This repository is a throughline *source*: a requirements graph, not a program. It
re-expresses the NIST AI RMF Generative AI Profile (NIST AI 600-1) as a grounded IDD graph
so consuming projects can compose it with throughline-compose. NIST AI 600-1 is a
cross-sectoral profile of the AI RMF: for the Subcategories where generative AI raises
distinct concerns it lists suggested Actions and the GenAI risks each Action helps address.

The AI RMF Function statements (each root intent's `text`), the Subcategory outcome
statements (each user_requirement's `text`) and the suggested-Action text (each
system_requirement's `text`), together with the GenAI risks carried in
`attrs.genai_risks`, are taken from:

  - NIST AI 600-1, Artificial Intelligence Risk Management Framework: Generative
    Artificial Intelligence Profile —
    https://www.nist.gov/itl/ai-risk-management-framework
    (NIST Trustworthy and Responsible AI, NIST AI 600-1)
  - NIST AI 100-1, Artificial Intelligence Risk Management Framework (AI RMF 1.0), for the
    four Function statements the Profile hangs its Actions onto —
    https://www.nist.gov/itl/ai-risk-management-framework

NIST AI 600-1 and the AI RMF 1.0 are works prepared by officers and employees of the
United States Government as part of their official duties and are therefore in the **public
domain** in the United States (17 U.S.C. Sec. 105). There is no copyright restriction on
